# Carrier-BSP env read by the tegraflash provisioner.
#
# The directory containing this file is overlaid on top of the MACHINE-baked
# tegraflash-bsp/ at provision time. A file placed here replaces the
# MACHINE-baked file of the same name, so a carrier-specific kernel DTB, BPMP
# DTB or BCT pinmux dtsi ships under the stock filename. No variable selects
# a different filename.
#
# The provisioner reads only the line forms below. Any other name is ignored
# without a warning, including CARRIER_DTB, CARRIER_BPF_DTB,
# CARRIER_PINMUX_DTSI, CARRIER_ODMDATA and CARRIER_KERNEL_ARGS_APPEND, which
# earlier revisions of this file documented but no provisioner implemented.

# CARRIER_LABEL: human-readable carrier ID for provisioning logs.
CARRIER_LABEL="jetson-orin-nano-devkit (P3768-0000 + P3767-0005)"

# CARRIER_FV_<NAME>=<value>: replace the existing <NAME>= line in the flashvars
# file with <NAME>="<value>". A <NAME> that has no line there is skipped with a
# warning; no line is added.
#
# CARRIER_ENV_<NAME>=<value>: the same rewrite in .env.initrd-flash, for
# example CARRIER_ENV_ODMDATA=<hex> for the UPHY lane mapping.
#
# A value must not contain a double quote, $, a backtick, a backslash or a
# newline: both target files are sourced by bash.
#
# Opt-in for a microSD slot behind an SD mux such as the SDWire3: uncomment
# to apply tegra234-p3767-sdmmc1-sdwire.dtbo (see the README). This replaces
# the machine's OVERLAY_DTB_FILE, which is empty for this target on the
# 2026/next feed (the only feed this was verified on).
# CARRIER_FV_OVERLAY_DTB_FILE="tegra234-p3767-sdmmc1-sdwire.dtbo"
#
# Kernel command line changes belong in the project's avocado.yaml
# (kernel.cmdline or kernel.cmdline_extra), not in this file.
